{"createdAt":"2026-10-30T05:16:53.211185+00:00","title":"Meiri on Pirkei Avot — Hebrew Wikisource edition","catalogPath":"Rabbinic/Meiri on Pirkei Avot (Hebrew Wikisource)","bibliographySourceLines":[1749,2276,2496],"sourceSeriesAuthorEvidence":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/w/index.php?title=%D7%9E%D7%90%D7%99%D7%A8%D7%99_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%94%D7%A9%22%D7%A1&oldid=3083958","sourceSnapshotPath":"Amudi/data/rights/additional-meiri-wiki-source-cache-20261030/page-cfaafcd23d7bef60.json","sourceSnapshotSha256":"fc395fc563d7fb56aa9cef6f5b719106228673e70bec7b86ddf7434cb553d373","finding":"The selected series identifies BeitHaBechira as Menachem benShlomo of theMeir family. The Ketubot/BavaBatra/Avot introductions explicitly name the author. No contrary authorship attribution was found in the inspected selected pages; this is not a survey of disputes beyond those source pages."},"license":"CC BY-SA4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","attribution":"Meiri on Pirkei Avot, Menachem Meiri (Menachem benShlomo HaMeiri). Typed digital edition and editorial notes by Hebrew Wikisource contributors, CC BY-SA4.0. Individual source revisions, source-page permalinks and contributor histories are recorded in source-manifest.json.","changes":"Amudi removed only source navigation and parser edit controls, image/style/script tags and parser attributes, and made source/reference links absolute. Ordinary reader chapters contain flat text/HTML strings and are bounded to16000plain characters /32000markup characters per group. Exceptionally long HTML blocks are converted to escaped plain-text chunks at whitespace boundaries; all selected reading text, notes, variants and explicit source gaps remain conserved in source order. No OCR or new translation. Copyrightable Amudi adaptations remain CC BY-SA4.0.","coverageScope":"The selected typed Avot introduction and five commentary chapter pages, followed by a separately labeled alternate typed excerpt for Avot3:14. Th